  "worked_solution": "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2x+{y}^{2} & =55+10y \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+({y}^{2}-10y) & =55 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =55+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 5y+{5}^{2}) & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-1))^{2}+(y-5)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,5)$ and its radius is $9.$",
